<title>USA: Texaco returning evacuated workers to rigs.</title>
<headline>Texaco returning evacuated workers to rigs.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Texaco Corp said it was moving about 365 workers back to 10 rigs in the U.S. Gulf and to several production platforms in the region after the workers were evacuated due to a hurricane there.</p>
<p>The workers were evacuated Thursday and resulted in Texaco shutting about 40,000 barrels per day of oil and about 200 million cubic feet of natural gas production.</p>
<p>&quot;We are starting to resume production that was shut, and we are putting our workers back on the facilities,&quot; said Pierre De Gruy Texaco spokesman in New Orleans, Louisiana.</p>
<p>&quot;We hope to have operations running normally during the weekend,&quot; added De Gruy.</p>
<p>Hurricane Danny was located about 55 miles east-southeast of New Orleans, Louisiana and about 90 miles southwest of Mobile, Alabama. Danny is moving toward the northeast at about five miles per hour (mph) with maximum sustained winds are near 75 mph.</p>
<p>-- New York Energy desk, 212-859-1620</p>
